   "title": "Boeing (Douglas Aircraft Company), DC-9 Airplane Characteristics for Airport Planning (June 1984, revised F 5/84), 2.2 General Airplane Dimensions: Model DC-9-51 and Model DC-9-32; 2.7.4 Passenger Entrance and Service Door Clearances, Model DC-9",
   "accessed": "2026-11-24",
   "note": "Dimensions and outlines read off the DC-9-51 sheet's side, plan and front views (tools/trace/dc95/), starting from the DC-9-30's points (tools/trace/dc93/) with its two plugs added; the figures are the aircraft's measurements, not a copy of the drawing. The sheet is a 1-bit scan on graph paper (about 47 px a meter at the scale rendered, so outlines are good to about 5 cm). Scaled by the printed 36.96 m from the nose to the tail cone. The wing, fin and tailplane are the DC-9-30's, snapped onto this sheet's drawing of them; the JT8D-17 nacelle with its later thrust reverser is this sheet's. Its side view draws the tube 3.52 m tall against the printed 3.61 m (its front view 3.57 m), so the fuselage is fit to the printed height (fit_height.py). The sheet draws 44 cabin windows (a dashed one at the aft end, optional, left out), the main entry door, two overwing exits a side and the cargo doors (dashed); the service door is placed from 2.7.4 as on the DC-9-30. Windows' height and width and the cockpit panes are the MD-80's (MD82: the same nose and cabin section). The nose strakes 2.7.4 notes on the DC-9-51 aren't drawn. Confidence medium: a scan."
  }
 ],
